course: dictionary
lesson: 3390
title: Expectancy: a feeling and a number
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Expectancy is a noun with two meanings. The first is the feeling that something exciting or important is about to happen. Stories often use the phrase «an air of expectancy», which tells you that everyone is waiting for something.
explain: The second meaning is about numbers. «Life expectancy» is the number of years a person or animal is likely to live, on average. When the words around it talk about years, countries or health, it is probably this second meaning.
explain: To choose the right meaning, use the context. Ask yourself: is someone waiting for something, or is the sentence counting years? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Expectancy means the feeling that something exciting or important is about to happen.
fact: «Life expectancy» means the number of years a person or animal is likely to live, on average.
fact: «An air of expectancy» means everyone in a place is waiting for something to happen.
fact: Average life expectancy in the world was about 32 years in 1900 and is about 73 today.
fact: Life expectancy has grown mostly because far fewer children die young.
exercise: The whole class sat with an air of expectancy as the teacher lifted the lid. What does expectancy mean here? | *The feeling that something exciting is about to happen | A number of years | A loud noise | A kind of box
exercise: «People in Japan live into their mid-80s on average, while in Chad life expectancy is in the 50s.» What does life expectancy mean? | The number of children in a family | *The number of years a person is likely to live, on average | The feeling of waiting for a surprise | The age of the oldest person in a school
exercise: Which phrase is about how long people live? | *life expectancy | a sense of expectancy | an air of expectancy | full of expectancy
test: Tom says life expectancy means how excited people feel about a birthday. Why is he wrong? | *Life expectancy is the number of years people are likely to live, on average | It means the same as expectancy in stories | It is about birthday parties and party food | Excitement is measured in years
test: «The air was full of expectancy before the fireworks.» What does expectancy mean here? | The number of years fireworks last | Being sad that the day is over | *The feeling that something exciting is about to happen | A type of loud bang
exam: In «Average life expectancy in the world was about 32 years in 1900 and is about 73 today», what does life expectancy mean? | *The number of years people are likely to live, on average | The number of children in each school | A type of world map | A feeling of waiting for something exciting
